{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1482028-how-to-create-servants-on-cof-2e","id":1482028,"title":"How to create servants on CoF 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-26T13:55:58-07:00","id":1482028,"title":"How to create servants on CoF 2e","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> This days I'm investigating on methods to Create (not invoke or control someone) servants: Homunculi, Golems, Abominations, Robot, etc!<br /> <br /> My search always led me to Classic World of Darkness, but I want to know 2e ways and alternatives, specially for splats like Mages, Vampire or Demons, but I would be happy with a Occult way.<br /> <br /> Someone has reference or help in this term?<br /> <br /> Also, before is mentioned: I now Prometheam have something with rules to create others prometheans, but for what I understand Azoth works very differently than other &quot;Power Attributes&quot; in that it can be expended or banked, not like Gnosis or Wyrd. But maybe I'm wrong and an aclararion can help.<br /> <br /> I need to clarify: I want advice and help with mechanics to create a servant in play as a character, not &quot;how to represent having one&quot; like &quot;mark them as a Retainer&quot;.<br /> <br /> If anyone have a Occult way, is the one I want the most, but any other splat being able to do is useful.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T15:11:22-07:00","id":1482030,"title":"","content":"Beasts (in the Beast\u2019s Player\u2019s Guide) have relatively in-depth rules for creating Horrorspawn, which are (reductively) tiny versions of the Beast\u2019s Horror.<br /> <br /> Mages have a few spells for minion creation. Death can raise zombies or create ghosts, Matter can create golems, Prime can create Eidolons (animate beings made from Mana), etc. With the right Arcana, you can go pretty wild. <br /> <br /> Changelings can use the \u201cDance of the Toys\u201d Contract to permanently animate object as a retainer. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, before is mentioned: I now Prometheam have something with rules to create others prometheans, but for what I understand Azoth works very differently than other &quot;Power Attributes&quot; in that it can be expended or banked, not like Gnosis or Wyrd. But maybe I'm wrong and an aclararion can help. </div> </div> </div>Azoth works much the same as other power stats. Prometheans have a separate \u201cfuel\u201d that they store and spend called Pyros, which is, in fact, used in the process of creating new Prometheans. It\u2019s possible for a mortal human to create a Promethean as well, but I don\u2019t remember if there are specific rules for that. Also, Prometheans don\u2019t make for great minions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 05-26-2022, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T16:03:30-07:00","id":1482033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1482028-how-to-create-servants-on-cof-2e#post1482028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My search always led me to Classic World of Darkness, but I want to know 2e ways and alternatives, specially for splats like Mages, Vampire or Demons, but I would be happy with a Occult way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires can create Gargoyles, for which official 1e mechanics exist in The Danse Macabre and unofficial 2e mechanics exist in the Storyteller's Vault product Wild Hunt: Gangrel.<br /> <br /> Demons can create cryptids out of animals through the Hellhounds Exploit.<br /> <br /> As mentioned, mages have options in many of their Arcana \u2014 the Life Arcanum bears emphasis for having core spells built to mix and match animal features on a creature, to highlight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, before is mentioned: I now Prometheam have something with rules to create others prometheans, but for what I understand Azoth works very differently than other &quot;Power Attributes&quot; in that it can be expended or banked, not like Gnosis or Wyrd. But maybe I'm wrong and an aclararion can help. </div> </div> </div>Closer to servants than Prometheans would be Pandorans, which result from failures to create Prometheans and can be controlled through the Lordship Alembic of the Flux category of Transmutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T01:30:29-07:00","id":1482063,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters (from <i>Geist: the Sin-Eaters</i>) can create a Homunculus out of their flesh and ectoplasm. It's a specific Haunt any Sin-Eater could theoretically learn (Disarticulation; Caul \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022). Another power can create Retainers out of representations (Terra Cotta Soldiers: Tomb \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022).<br /> <br /> <i>Mummy: the Curse</i> introduced Amkhata (singular: Amkhat). They're chimerical abominations made of animal body parts and corrupt sorcery. Anyone, be it a Mummy or a Mortal can learn to make one, but controlling them takes skill or Occult know-how.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 05-27-2022, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T01:10:57-07:00","id":1482227,"title":"","content":"Ultimately the answer is explain what you want to your ST and put aside the xp to pay for it.<br /> Vampire has birthing the god (I think it\u2019s called) in Secrets of the Covenants.<br /> If you\u2019re the ST and trying to make something for a NPC to do it\u2019s much simpler since you don\u2019t need to balance it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}